{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774721,"nonce":"tB0gmTR+fXCxElpXHuAiwRqIihs=","title":"fix(environments): stamp canonical secret_scope/oidc_subject server-side","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #39 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `fix/env-create-derived-fields` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-19T18:58:20Z · Merged: 2026-07-20T04:50:34Z\n\n\nCreating an environment from the web UI failed with a 400:\n\n```\nFailed to deserialize the JSON body into the target type: missing field `secret_scope` at line 1 column 85\n```\n\nThe **New environment** form (`RepoView.tsx`) posts only `approvers`, `wait_timer`, `allowed_refs`, `concurrency`. But `PUT …/environments/{name}` deserialized the body straight into `scarab_project::ProtectionRules`, which also had two **required** fields: `secret_scope` and `oidc_subject`. Serde rejected the body at the first missing one.\n\n\nBoth fields are **write-only and fully derivable** from the environment's `(org, repo, name)` coordinate — nothing in the runtime ever reads them:\n\n- secret resolution re-derives the scope from the path via the `secret_scope()` helper;\n- the OIDC subject is minted fresh at run time via `Claims::run_subject(...)`.\n\nAsking the client to supply them was wrong on principle, not just a form omission.\n\n\nMade both fields **server-authoritative**:\n\n1. `scarab-project` — both now `#[serde(default)]` (with a small placeholder fn for `SecretScope`, which has no `Default`), so a body may omit them.\n2. `scarab-server` — `put_environment` **stamps** the canonical values from the path (`secret_scope = Environment{org,repo,name}`, `oidc_subject = scarab:org/{org}/repo/{repo}/env/{name}`). This also closes a small hole — a caller can no longer inject a bogus scope/subject.\n3. Regression test sending the exact body the UI form sends, asserting the server stamps both fields.\n\nNo UI change needed — its `ProtectionRules` TS type already declared only the four fields.\n\n\n- `cargo check --workspace` — green.\n- `cargo test -p scarab-project` — green.\n- The new HTTP test is Postgres-gated (`SCARAB_TEST_DATABASE_URL`); it compiles and runs, skipping cleanly without a DB. Run against real Postgres (e.g. the `just` stack) for the end-to-end assertion.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}